$A7AD ; AT (18,23), attribute $45 (cyan): then ShowOrder prints OrderLine
$A7B2 t OrderLine ; The order's name, 27 bytes copied from OrderNames: the image holds STOP AND DEFEND
> Filled by ShowOrder before each print; the copied name brings its own end byte 0. The block was saved from a running game, so the buffer holds the last name copied into it, order 0's "  STOP  ", "  AND   ", " DEFEND " (code 3 between the lines), the same bytes as the first name of OrderNames.
$A7B2 ; the order's three 8-character lines and the end 0, copied from OrderNames by ShowOrder

$A7CD c ShowOrderMiles ; Robot menu: for ADVANCE and RETREAT, the miles under the order's name
> Orders 1 and 2 only: prints at (19,25) the distance +$0E / 2 with two digits (PrintNumber2), into the blank middle line of the order's name ("ADVANCE", "nn", "MILES"). Other orders jump straight to RobotMenuChoose. IX = the robot record.
> The printing tail after the inline position is ShowMilesCode ($A7DC).
