@module gameturn ; the game turn: the clock, daily production, capture, the game end and the turn pacing
@about The second half of every pass of the play loop and of every robot menu loop: WorldTurn moves the robots and shots, GameTurn then keeps the time and the rules that are not a robot's.
@about In calling order: GameTurn steps Random and the clock (+5 minutes a turn; a new day runs DailyProduction, which runs ProduceSide and AddCapped for both sides; PrintInline prints the clock position and GameTurnEnd prints the days and HH.MM; CheckGameEnd ends the game when a side has no warbase (GameWon or the lost message, then GameStop and GameOverWait back to Start; CaptureLoop counts the turns a robot stands on each of the 28 base doors and hands a base over at 144 (GiveWarbase / GiveFactory, then CountBases and UpdateStatusPanel; TurnPace waits until a turn has lasted 10 frames.
@about Data it owns or keeps: Clock ($FD35: minutes, hours, the 16-bit day count), TurnFrames ($FD34, counted up by PlayInterrupt), the capture counters (+4 of each 5-byte record in Warbases $FD70 / Factories $FD84), the resources of both sides (Resources, EnemyResources) through the building counts PlayerBuildings / EnemyBuildings (docs 10.2, 10.7, 10.10).
@about Tricks: PrintInline reads the print codes after the CALL (ClockPos, LostText, WonText) and returns past them, so the code goes on behind the text. The lost path (LostJump: JR GameOverWait) and the won path meet in GameOverWait; UnusedTapeCode is never-run dead code between the routines.
$AD62 c GameTurn ; One game turn: the random step, the clock, the daily production, the clock print
> Random steps the random generator $FD00-$FD03. Clock ($FD35 minutes, $FD36 hours, $FD37-$FD38 days) gains 5 minutes a turn: 60 minutes make an hour, 24 hours a day, and a new day runs DailyProduction. Then the clock print: days at (0,27), five digits with leading spaces; "HH.MM" on the next line. Goes on in GameTurnEnd.
