@module bases ; the bases: counts, owners, buildings, destruction and the new game's map
@about The 28 capture points (4 warbases, 24 factories) and what stands on them: their 5-byte records in Warbases ($FD70) and Factories ($FD84), the 56 building records of Buildings ($FF01: pads, factory roofs, flags) and the map blocks they are drawn from.
@about The counts: CountBases (PlayerBuildings $FD3A / EnemyBuildings $FD42, 7 each: warbases, then the six factory kinds) after every change of owner; CountRobots with CountLiveRobots (PlayerRobotCount $FD41 / EnemyRobotCount $FD49) after every birth and death.
@about The owners: GiveFactory and GiveWarbase (from the capture tick and BuildMap) set the owner bits through SetBaseOwner, which falls into BaseCell (the door cell), and move the flags and the pad: RemoveBuilding / AddBuilding. The destruction: DestroyFactory and DestroyWarbase (from NuclearBlast) mark the record $80 (MarkBaseDestroyed), remove the buildings and redraw the base's shape in debris (DrawRuins).
@about The map: BuildMap, once a new game, clears the map and the radar, places the scenery lists (PlaceScenery) and the base lists (PlaceBases), gives warbase 0 to the player and 1-3 to the enemy, counts and puts the ship on. The block layer under them: DrawShape walks a shape of ShapeTable, StepCell moves by a signed step, PutBlock writes one 2 x 2 block (its anchor plain, the other three cells with bit 5).
@about Positions relative to a base's door cell (x, y): a factory's roof row is y-2 (its building at x, our flag at x-2, the enemy's at x+2), a warbase's pad row y-4 (the pad at x, our flag at x-4, the enemy's at x+4). A map row is $200 bytes, so the code moves rows with DEC H / INC H in pairs.
$BB09 c CountBases ; Count each side's bases: warbases and the factories of each type
> Clears PlayerBuildings ($FD3A, 7 counts) and EnemyBuildings ($FD42, 7) and goes through the 28 base records ($FD70, 5 bytes, read at +3): a base whose +3 has bit 6 counts for the player, bit 5 for the enemy, at index +3 bits 0-2 (0 warbases, 1-6 the factories of type 1-6: electronics, nuclear, phasers, missiles, cannon, chassis, the resource each makes; neutral and destroyed (bit 7) bases do not count. PlayerRobotCount ($FD41) between the two count blocks is skipped. The status panel shows these counts ($D2C1; the daily production ($AE38) adds 5 general per warbase and 2 per factory to its resource; a side with no warbase loses ($AE6B).
> Called after every change of owner (the capture tick $AE17), after the blast ($BA81), and by the map builder ($BCCA). A, B, DE, HL lost.
