@module mainmenu ; The room of the main menu and LOAD MAP, the redefine-keys screen
@about NE's main menu, its tape save and load of a game, are gone: $C100-$C334 is zero in the block. Stage 3 fills two parts of it with pieces of the patches block (src/patches99): $C100-$C17E with the menu piece (menu128 or menu48: jumps for the start-up menu, which itself runs at $D800 on 128 K, copied from page 1) and $C1FD-$C332 with LOAD MAP (diskmap or tapemap). Start ($A600) calls $C100; the start-up menu's LOAD MAP item jumps to $C1FD. $C17F-$C1FC and $C333-$C334 stay zero; the byte $C335 is the last of NE's WaitAnyKey (RET).
@about What is left of NE's code here is the redefine-keys screen, called by the start-up menu (the item under the three control options, CALL $C34A at `$DA77`), which also sets Controls ($D3E4) for KEYBOARD, KEMPSTON J/S and INTERFACE 2 ($DA71) and colours them through ControlsOptionAttr. The screen now asks seven keys: after ABORT, ReadAbortKey writes a fixed record for the SAVE key (ENTER) and returns, with no wait for the key's release.
@about The redefine screen does not use KeyTable to read: DefineKey reads the keyboard with the ROM's KEY-SCAN ($028E) and the ROM's key table ($0205). RedefineKeys clears and refills KeyTable (module controls) through DefineKey: a key value E becomes the 3-byte record (port high byte, bit mask, code) ReadControls reads.
@about Inline strings everywhere: a CALL PrintInline is followed by its text (position, attribute and size codes, then characters, 0), and execution goes on after the 0. PrintKeyPrompt ends in JP PrintInline, so the key name after each CALL PrintKeyPrompt is a string too; the checks for SYM SH / ENTER / CAPS SH / SPACE each put a RET after their name string. DefineKeyDone ($C4A6) is also command 0 of the music tables.
$C100 s MenuPieceRoom ; Zero: stage 3 copies the start-up menu's piece here (menu128 or menu48)
> The 127 bytes $C100-$C17E. On 128 K stage 3 copies the patches block's menu128 piece here ($6340), on one page or the tape path menu48 ($6329): a table of jumps whose first, `JP $C112` / the 48 K one, is the start-up menu Start calls. The block's zeros never run.
$C17F s MainMenuSpare ; Zero, never written: NE's main menu keys, title and load code were here
> $C17F-$C1FC: nothing writes or reads these bytes in the '99 program.

$C1FD s LoadMapRoom ; Zero: stage 3 copies LOAD MAP here (diskmap from disk, tapemap on the tape path)
> The 310 bytes $C1FD-$C332, the size of the disk piece; the tape piece takes 147. The start-up menu's LOAD MAP item jumps to $C1FD; the piece reads a NELEV file, copies its lists over $BDA9-$BF9B and its tail into the game's operands (src/res/maps/README.md), then jumps to Start.
$C333 b WaitAnyKeyEnd 3 ; Two zeros and $C9, the RET that ended NE's WaitAnyKey
> Never run: nothing calls $C325 any more.

$C336 c ControlsOptionAttr ; The attribute for menu option C: cyan ($45) when it is the current Controls, else yellow ($46)
> C = the option's Controls value (1-3). Prints an inline attribute code: $45 (cyan, bright) when Controls ($D3E4) is C, else $46 (yellow, bright; the option text printed next takes it. Called by the three option entries before their text; A and the flags are lost.
